This project includes code adapted from:

  seifghazi/claude-code-proxy
  https://github.com/seifghazi/claude-code-proxy
  commit 02c9c766679eee75c861bbde11c6d8b5249d44a7

used under the MIT License reproduced in full below, with its copyright
notice.

Adapted portions live in internal/proxy and cmd/splitter/cmd_proxy.go. The
upstream project's pass-through forwarding and SSE streaming approach
(originally internal/handler/handlers.go and internal/provider/anthropic.go
in the upstream project) was restructured around splitter's own SQLite
schema (internal/store), an async logger goroutine with fail-open
behaviour, repo HEAD capture, and a session id heuristic. The upstream
project's web dashboard, conversation browser and model router were not
used; splitter has no web UI (see BRIEF.md, "Non-goals").

Every Go source file adapted from the upstream project carries a header
comment identifying it: "Adapted from seifghazi/claude-code-proxy (MIT),
commit 02c9c766."

